        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f254cabc-159c-53fc-82a4-be9bbdc51909",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Prince, Space Cowboy, Martin Kierszenbaum, RedOne\n- Groups: The Revolution, Cinema Bizarre\n- Works: \"I Would Die 4 U\", Purple Rain, ToyZ, BANG!, \"I Came 2 Party\"\n- Topics: singles, cover versions, soundtrack albums\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Prince released Purple Rain as his sixth studio album, the first album to feature The Revolution, and the soundtrack to the 1984 film of the same name.\n- In 1984, Prince and The Revolution released \"I Would Die 4 U\" as the fourth U.S. single from Purple Rain.\n- Purple Rain has sold over 25 million copies worldwide, making it the third-best-selling soundtrack album of all time.\n- In 2002, Dresti changed his stage name to Space Cowboy and recorded a cover of Prince's \"I Would Die 4 U.\"\n- In 2009, Cinema Bizarre included \"I Came 2 Party,\" featuring Space Cowboy, on ToyZ and on their debut U.S. album BANG!.\n- Martin Kierszenbaum, RedOne, and Space Cowboy wrote and produced \"I Came 2 Party.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
